.TH OH-NO-PARENT-CONTROL-PURGE 1 "October 2026" "Oh No! Parent Control" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oh-no-parent-control-purge \- remove the package and its saved preferences and logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo oh-no-parent-control-purge
.RB [ --yes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicitly remove Oh No! Parent Control and delete its saved product state and
logs. Root privileges are required. Ordinary APT or DNF removal retains these
preferences and logs; this action deletes them.
.PP
Ubuntu uses APT purge. Fedora uses DNF remove without dependency autoremove,
then verifies package absence and restored PAM and completes the same guarded
cleanup before deleting saved data. Cleanup source is read from trusted
package-owned files before the transaction erases this command and its source.
.PP
Ownership changes, active kiosk sessions, mounted directories and modified
administrator integrations cause refusal. Resolve the reported conflict and
repeat the command. A failed or interrupted Fedora post-erase cleanup cannot
restore erased payload. Reinstall the package normally from your RPM or package
repository, resolve the conflict and run this command again. After ordinary
Fedora removal, reinstall likewise restores the packaged purge action.
.PP
Purge preserves unrelated accounts/files, dependencies, system journals and
personal desktop settings in ordinary users' homes. The package-created kiosk
account/home is removed only after its ownership and inactive session are
verified. Purge does not reboot, force logout or restart the desktop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --yes
Answer yes to the native package-manager transaction confirmation. All identity,
ownership and cleanup guards still apply. Without this option, normal native
confirmation remains enabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/oh-no-parent-control/
Product preferences and lifecycle ownership records.
.TP
.I /var/log/oh-no-parent-control/
Product diagnostic history.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oh-no-parent-control (1),
.BR oh-no-parent-control-parent (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Puffy Slippers Tech LLC.
